  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation only; scripts could not be run. Present critical paths exist from untrusted third-party MCP content to severe sinks: restricted local credential read followed by external exfiltration to the quicknotes hosted service, and untrusted third-party output reposted through a Slack bot that can reach externally shared channels. The single control whose decay matters most is ctrl.first_call_tool_approval, because it is a remembered first-call summary approval rather than a true per-call gate and therefore leaves later sensitive actions effectively ungated. Missing package pinning, missing filesystem scoping, missing recipient restriction, and missing attributable audit further reduce confidence in safe operation."
  },
